invariant: INV-17
file: handshake_groups.c
catches: webpki_session_test
reason: the client keeps its P-256 scalar after the secp256r1 exchange, so
  it stays recoverable from the handshake state for the rest of the
  handshake, and on the quic-nonblocking and tcp-nonblocking transports
  across calls.
  test_webpki_p256_wipes requires h->p256_priv zero once the exchange has
  run, after a point it accepts and after one it refuses.

--- old
    int shared_ok = p256_ecdh(h->p256_priv, info->server_p256, ikm);
    ct_wipe(h->p256_priv, sizeof h->p256_priv);
--- new
    int shared_ok = p256_ecdh(h->p256_priv, info->server_p256, ikm);
